{"authored" [{"question" "q-130292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/state.json" "file_sha256" "d53c0281f12463ce2db5b2adef4fe688a42354c25096c2e46e3e49ddeb4fcd5d" "basis" 1594 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the $3$rd column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot 5\\cdot 6\\cdot (-1)=-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-60.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/state.json" "file_sha256" "d53c0281f12463ce2db5b2adef4fe688a42354c25096c2e46e3e49ddeb4fcd5d" "basis" 1594 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" 